2,100,19],[32468,29.3,1952,64,100,19],[32469,34.2,1973,66,101,18],[32767,54.4,1952,62,114,20],[32768,42.6,1973,66,106,21],[33067,44.0,1952,67,111,25],[33068,51.8,1973,62,104,27]],"links":[["Powell County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/montana/powell-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 19 grids June to July, July to August, August to September and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 35 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 65% of normal in May to June and 67% in June to July. July to August is the driest pair at 2.55 inches of normal, and May to June the wettest at 5.34. Grid 31868 had its driest year in 1960 at 64%.</p>"}
